==English==
{{was wotd|2023|November|7}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰerǵʰ-|*dʰerǵʰ-|*dʰeh₁-}}
From Late {{inh|en|enm|fortifien}}, {{m|enm|fortfien|t=to strengthen (a castle, etc.) from attack; to strengthen (an army, etc.); to strengthen (a person), aid, support; to reinforce, support; to improve; to increase the efficacy of}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=fortifīen|pos=v|id=MED17284}}</ref> from {{der|en|fro|fortifier}} (modern {{cog|fr|fortifier}}), from {{der|en|LL.|fortificō|fortificāre|to strengthen, fortify}}, from {{der|en|la|fortis|t=powerful, strong}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰerǵʰ-|t=to ascend, rise up; to be elevated or up high}} or {{m|ine-pro|*dʰerǵʰ-|t=to be firm; robust, strong}}) + {{m|la|-ficō|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming {{glossary|causative}} or {{glossary|factitive}}, or other {{glossary|verb}}s}}.<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=5156362693|date=September 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref>

